---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import IntakeForm from '../components/IntakeForm.astro';
import HeroBanner from '../components/HeroBanner.astro';
import RequirementsIntakeCta from '../components/RequirementsIntakeCta.astro';
import ResearchClusterNav from '../components/ResearchClusterNav.astro';

const title = 'Portugal HQA Visa University - Academic Affiliation Pathway';
const metaTitle = `${title} | Portugal HQA Residency`;
const metaDescription =
  'Portugal HQA visa university affiliation in 2026 is an academic host path, not a degree visa. See how a university contract is tested for HQA eligibility.';
---

<Layout title={metaTitle} description={metaDescription}>
  <article>
    <header>
      <HeroBanner
        image="/images/portugal-hqa-visa-university-campus.jpg"
        alt="White modernist courtyard walls with dark door openings and a small dome catching late sun"
        title={title}
        items={[
          { href: '/', label: 'Home' },
          { href: '/portugal-hqa-visa', label: 'Portugal HQA Visa' },
          { href: '/portugal-research-visa', label: 'Research visa' },
          { label: 'University' },
        ]}
      />
      <div class="bg-background">
        <div class="site-container py-24 md:py-32">
        <p class="max-w-3xl">
          Portugal HQA visa university affiliation is the academic-host path: a Portuguese university or related institute as employer or contracting host for highly qualified activity. It is not a student visa, not an Erasmus stay, and not a visiting-scholar invitation on its own. Searchers who typed “research visa” should start at
          <a href="/portugal-research-visa" class="inline-link">Portugal research visa</a>,
          then confirm
          <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-eligibility" class="inline-link">HQA visa eligibility</a>
          for the post.
        </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-background-alt">
      <div class="site-container max-w-3xl py-24 md:py-32">
        <section>
          <h2>Academic staff versus students</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            Lecturers, researchers on institute contracts, and other specialists hired to work are in a different category from people enrolled to study. A PhD enrolment letter, a tuition receipt, or a student residence heading is not this pathway. The university must be the host for professional activity that meets the highly qualified tests in force in 2026.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>

    <RequirementsIntakeCta
      source="/portugal-hqa-visa-university"
      image="/images/portugal-hqa-visa-university-cta-divider.jpg"
      alt="Portuguese university courtyard used on the HQA university page"
      heading="Match a university appointment to highly qualified activity"
      copy="Not sure whether academic staff or a student stay is the right heading? Enter your details and our advisory team can help point you in the right direction."
    />

    <div class="bg-background-alt">
      <div class="site-container max-w-3xl py-24 md:py-32">
        <section>
          <h2>What the appointment has to show</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            A usable pack names the Portuguese institution, the role, the duration, and pay or maintenance. An informal email from a faculty member is not a contract. Title inflation (“visiting professor” on a business card) does not replace the statutory tests. Those tests are on
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-eligibility" class="inline-link">who qualifies</a>.
            Salary floors, where they apply to the contract type, still apply.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-24">
          <h2>When the host is a funded project instead</h2>
          <p class="mt-6">
            If the person is attached to a named grant or laboratory work package rather than to an academic appointment, use the
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa-research-project" class="inline-link">HQA visa research project</a>
            pathway. The program overview remains the
            <a href="/portugal-hqa-visa" class="inline-link">Portugal HQA visa</a>
            guide.
          </p>
        </section>

        <ResearchClusterNav current="/portugal-hqa-visa-university" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="bg-cta-tint">
      <div class="site-container flex flex-col items-start gap-6 py-24 md:py-32">
        <h2 class="max-w-3xl">Match the university contract to highly qualified activity, not to the campus name</h2>
        <p class="max-w-2xl">
          This page is informational. It is not legal, tax, or immigration advice. Academic titles and contract forms differ. A licensed professional should read the appointment against the current AIMA and consular list.
        </p>
        {/* TODO: no backend yet */}
        <IntakeForm source="/portugal-hqa-visa-university" simple />
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
